      "protocol": "visit (slot 0x64eafb0) expands the seed into a 0x58-byte state at [rsp+0x20]; a dword tag of 5 there ends the walk before any allocation.  next (slot 0x64eaf10) yields the first element record at [rsp+0x78]; a qword tag of 5 there also ends it.  Both terminal cases store the empty header {0, 8, 0} to the output and return it.  Otherwise the function allocates 0x160 bytes, stores the first element verbatim, initialises the header {capacity 4, buffer, count 1} on its stack, copies the input descriptor record's first 0x38 bytes into a stack cursor at [rsp+0xd0], and loops: visit expands the cursor into a state at [rsp+0x108] (dword tag 5 ends), next yields the next element at [rsp+0x20] (qword tag 5 ends), the element is appended verbatim at stride 0x58, growing through 0x474e640 when count == capacity.  The finished header {capacity, buffer, count} is stored to the first argument and returned in rax.  The input record is consumed as the cursor seed only: no field of it is copied into any element or into the output header.",
