      "transformation": "The function overwrites its first argument (the descriptor record) in place and returns it: word +0x00 and word +0x08 are configuration outputs (each 0 or 1 on the traced arms), word +0x10 is the slot-object address 0x6500060 when the second record's +0x10 byte is 1 and the global-table address 0x64fe408 otherwise, word +0x18 is the second record's word +0x00 (or, when that is 0, a fresh 0x30-byte heap copy of the default record produced through slot 0x64e12f8), word +0x20 is the second record's word +0x08 (or the static 0x6495038 on the default arm), and byte +0x28 is the configuration flag -- on the default arm the second record's +0x11 byte XOR 1.  The second record itself is only read (words +0x00/+0x08 and bytes +0x10/+0x11); it is neither stored into the output beyond those words nor freed.  The configuration lookup consults the once-initialised state at 0x64fdbe0 (initialiser 0x4752c90), the config byte at 0x64fdbe8, the table at 0x64fe408 with its dword at 0x64fe440 (initialiser 0x5c6c15a), and isatty(1)/isatty(2) through GLOB_DAT slot 0x64eaf90 on the arms where the consulted byte is 0.",
