  "phase2_verdict": "The phase-2 probe's two branches emit the same descriptor record into the same collect call: the record builds and the string boxing are byte-identical outside displacement fields decoding to the same targets, and the collect function turns the record into a vector of streamed 0x58-byte element records whose header lands at [rsp+0x90] on both branches.  The sentinel (capacity == 0x8000000000000000) branch then binds the descriptor in place through 0x47473c0 (slot 0x64e1458) and stores a 0x30-byte copy under tag 0x63ffbf8; the non-sentinel branch formats the found entry's stored text through the format consumer with the '_overflow{}' piece, emits through 0x473c130 (slot 0x64e1460), inserts the descriptor through 0x156f680, and stores a 0x70-byte snapshot under tag 0x63ffc70.  The branch therefore changes the destination and the downstream emissions, not the descriptor record or the collect result.",
  "phase2_limits": "Static trace only.  The functions behind slots 0x64eafb0 (stream visit, 5,696 bytes) and 0x64eaf10 (stream next, 3,781 bytes) are hash-pinned boundaries: how they expand the cursor, whether the visit function mutates the cursor in place between loop iterations, and which element records a given descriptor produces are NOT traced.  The bind function's configuration outputs are modelled under the file-initial global values (state 0, config byte 3, table dword 3), under which neither isatty arm is reached for the consumer's call; runtime mutation of those globals by other callers, and the exact outputs on the isatty arms, are NOT traced.  The descriptor-emit function behind slot 0x64e1460 (1,295 bytes), the map insert 0x156f680 (4,969 bytes), the second-tree insert 0x1497040 (3,092 bytes), the grow helper, the two collect cleanup helpers, the two bind initialisers, and the default-record producer are hash-pinned boundaries; the producer is itself the third direct caller of the collect function (0x473a03b), which is recorded as census, not traced.  The format consumer is the RE-015 owner traced by #2408 and is a boundary here.  What the second structure's readers do with the two payload kinds (tag 0x63ffbf8 versus tag 0x63ffc70), and who consumes the vector the collect call leaves at [rsp+0x90] after phase 2, are the next questions.  No captured code executed, no runtime value beyond the pinned file-initial globals, or reconstruction gate is claimed."
}
